From 6f7f9ffc88843497b46be784cf77cb22644e3488 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zak Winnick <zak@winnick.io>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 18:09:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Redesign the website to match the iOS app

Bring the site into the app's visual language: grouped grey ground,
white rounded cards, system type, the forest accent and per-type colors.

- Map is the home page on every screen size; the phone view opens on the map
- Header uses the app's four tabs (Locations, Map, Saved, Browse) as a
  floating capsule; on phones it becomes the bottom tab bar
- New All Locations photo gallery at /locations/ with search and type filters
- Browse hub at /regions/ for types, states and secondary pages
- Location pages rebuilt around a photo, title, and app-style cards
- Map markers draw the type symbols instead of text glyphs; the camera
  frames places beside the floating finder panel
- Eyebrow labels and tagline headings removed

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PLeEuAjfQ3D9DCGZU9SXrq
